      "text": "I think almost everything about my $AXTI thesis from 2025 was validated? \n\nFrom AXT's position in the InP substrate bottleneck... Being able to threaten the hyperscaler buildout (per Reuters)... \n\n$IQE has been flagging this as a major risk, VPEC and Taiwan epiwafer foundries have been crying over InP substrate bottlenecks. \n\nAnd there's even AXT direct confirmation of partnerships with $LITE and $COHR as the InP substrate supplier. AXT also stated $130m/quarter InP revenue capacity exiting 2027 (~$520m annualized) so that's a massive revenue inflection compared to previously. \n\nNow... the big",
